                <pb facs="0586" n="520" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg520"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1731/71a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Nicaragua</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-09-28T18:00:00-04:00">September 28, 1934—6
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Telegraph whether proposed trade agreement with the United States will
                    require ratification by legislature and if so when next session will be
                    inaugurated and duration. Repeat to other missions in Central America.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
